okay today I'm going to talk to you  about natural selection natural  selection is basically the driving force  behind evolution so it's how a species  change over millions of years to become  new species so the first stage is the  idea that we have different organisms  born that have variation so here I have  two rabbits apologies for my bad join  that have that are born with variation  so within a population  there is always variation variation just  means variety differences so some  rabbits might be born with small is and  some rabbits might be born with big is  there's just that natural variation  between members of the same species now  the important thing is that the  variation between species could give one  of them a survival advantage now what  that means is this one here might be  more likely to survive because it has  better hearing so it has a survival  advantage so if I imagine I have a Fox  coming along right here again apologies  for my terrible drawing Fox coming along  I could see that this one is more likely  to hear the Fox comment and is more  likely to escape whereas this one is  less likely to hear the Fox come in so  it's more likely to get eaten so I could  see that this one would get eaten and  this one would survive that natural  variation has given a survival advantage  this means that this rabbit here with  the gene for slightly longer ears is  more likely to be able to reproduce to  produce more rabbits also with those  bigger ears  as well so we can see this is how  natural selection works we have the idea  of variation between members of the same  species we have a particular  characteristic that provides a survival  advantage because of that characteristic  they are more likely to survive  therefore they're more likely to  reproduce and therefore that gene so the  gene here for the bigger is is more  likely to be passed on to the next  generation to their offspring now this  process is not a fast process this  process can take millions and millions  of years it can take many many hundreds  of thousands of different generations  but that is the main mechanism behind it  so just to summarize natural selection  is how it's basically the driving force  behind evolution it's how we have  changing in organisms over a period of  time it's based on variation between a  population a particular characteristic  providing a survival advantage therefore  that particular gene be more likely to  be passed on to the offspring because  that individual has lived long enough to  be able to reproduce apologies for the  Fox and thank you very much
 

